00:00:29.444 --> 00:00:31.073
So we'll have to see.

00:00:31.073 --> 00:00:32.822
I'm sorry to the person on the other side.

00:00:32.822 --> 00:00:34.320
This is weird.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:36.340
I'm like trying to test out her knuckles

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:39.799
I'm like, is that Saf's knuckles
or is that somebody else's?

00:00:39.799 --> 00:00:42.289
But then again, I don't even
know what Safiya's knuckles

00:00:42.289 --> 00:00:44.076
feel like, so I don't even
know why I'm trying that.

00:00:44.076 --> 00:00:45.935
There's a little bit of
gamesmanship going on here.

00:00:45.935 --> 00:00:47.759
I think that part of you
guys might have been like

00:00:47.759 --> 00:00:49.767
let's put Safiya first, trick out Tyler.

00:00:52.747 --> 00:00:54.366
Oh, this is tricky now.

00:00:55.466 --> 00:00:58.475
Now this hand is a little bit bigger

00:00:58.475 --> 00:01:00.563
and Safiya's got pretty big hands.

00:01:04.023 --> 00:01:05.310
This is impossible.

00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:06.270
(laughs)

00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:11.359
I'm in pretty intense thought right now,

00:01:11.359 --> 00:01:13.596
but this feels like a hand that I know.

00:01:15.216 --> 00:01:17.281
It's like the warmth a little bit

00:01:17.281 --> 00:01:18.896
and I'm adding in some descriptors

00:01:18.896 --> 00:01:21.264
which can only hurt me if I'm wrong.

00:01:21.264 --> 00:01:24.383
I'm like, this hand feels
like a hand I've been holding.

00:01:25.933 --> 00:01:27.682
Okay, this is Safiya's hand.

00:01:27.682 --> 00:01:31.324
I think Safiya's hand is number three

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:33.209
and I'm really hoping that it is

00:01:33.209 --> 00:01:34.693
because I'm pretty nervous right now.

00:01:37.914 --> 00:01:39.672
No, who is that?

00:01:41.273 --> 00:01:42.492
It's two then.

00:01:45.112 --> 00:01:46.789
Oh my god!

00:01:48.049 --> 00:01:50.643
No, I thought I would have known.

00:01:51.416 --> 00:01:53.281
I don't want to see, she's gonna be mad.

00:01:55.316 --> 00:01:57.035
- Are you serious?

00:01:57.035 --> 00:01:58.916
I would've been so good at this.

00:01:58.916 --> 00:01:59.706
- No, stop.

00:01:59.706 --> 00:02:01.586
It was not that easy,
I couldn't really tell.

00:02:01.586 --> 00:02:03.235
- He did horribly.

00:02:03.235 --> 00:02:06.565
Why did you think that the
first hand was not my hand?

00:02:06.565 --> 00:02:09.620
- We don't walk this far
apart, is really what it is.

00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:12.280
So, we usually walk
right next to each other

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:14.091
and so we're farther apart,
it just felt different.

00:02:14.091 --> 00:02:15.112
Like the angle was different.

00:02:15.112 --> 00:02:16.551
- No, it's fine.

00:02:16.551 --> 00:02:19.812
I'm not mad, I'm just disappointed.

00:02:19.812 --> 00:02:22.912
- Listen, I've held one hand for a year

00:02:22.912 --> 00:02:24.887
and maybe if other people get them then

00:02:24.887 --> 00:02:26.768
